     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of h3_0:access, h3_1:reach and h3_2:reach, so all three must be cut off. Blocking h1_1:access removes h3_2:reach, since h1_1 is its only parent. It also removes h3_1:reach, an AND that needs h1_1. Blocking h3_0:access removes the last path, which is otherwise reachable via h1_0:reach or h2_1:reach from the entries. One block is not enough: no single blockable step lies on every path. Blocking h3_0 leaves h3_2 open, and blocking h1_1 leaves h3_0 reachable through h1_0. So the minimum is 2.\"}"
